<title>UKRAINE: Ukraine Jan-March trade deficit widens to $1.23 bl.</title>
<headline>Ukraine Jan-March trade deficit widens to $1.23 bl.</headline>
<dateline>KIEV 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ukraine's trade deficit widened to $1.24 billion in the first three months of this year from $607 million in January-February 1997, the Statistics Ministry said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>UKRAINE MERCHANDISE TRADE  Jan-March 97 Jan-Feb 97 Jan-March 96</p>
<p> Exports (bln $)		2.922	  1.879	2.559</p>
<p> Imports (bln $)		4.158	  2.487	3.112</p>
<p> Balance (bln $)	     -1.235	 -0.607     -0.553</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are for trade with all countries. Trade with former Soviet republics resulted in a deficit of $1.6 billion.</p>
<p>--Kiev newsroom, +380 44 244 9150</p>
